window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-54bcd8fe7e7104d7"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-for-macos\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"macos\">为 macOS 构建应用</h1> <p>使用 Codex 和 SwiftUI 搭建、构建并调试原生 Mac 应用。</p> <p>使用 Codex 构建 macOS SwiftUI 应用，接入以 shell 为先的构建与运行循环，并在应用逐渐成熟时加入原生桌面场景、窗口、AppKit 和签名工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>希望 Codex 搭建原生桌面应用框架和可重复构建脚本的全新 macOS SwiftUI 项目。</li> <li>需要 Codex 处理窗口、菜单、侧边栏、设置、AppKit 互操作或签名问题的现有 Mac 应用。</li> <li>希望 macOS 开发以 shell 为先、同时遵循原生桌面体验惯例的团队。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-macos-apps（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用以 shell 为先的工作流构建和调试 macOS 应用；设计原生桌面 SwiftUI 场景和窗口；在需要时桥接 AppKit；并准备签名和公证流程。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>界面框架</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI（需联网）</a></td> <td>适合构建窗口、侧边栏、工具栏、设置和由场景驱动的 Mac 应用结构。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>AppKit 桥接</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AppKit（需联网）</a></td> <td>仅在 SwiftUI 无法完整表达所需桌面行为时，使用小型 <code>NSViewRepresentable</code>、<code>NSViewControllerRepresentable</code> 或 <code>NSWindow</code> 桥接。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>构建与打包</td> <td><code>xcodebuild</code>、<code>swift build</code> 和 <a href=\"https://asccli.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Store Connect CLI（需联网）</a></td> <td>让本地构建、手动归档、脚本化公证和 App Store 上传都能通过可重复的终端优先流程完成。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>搭建原生 Mac 应用</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Build macOS Apps 插件搭建一个基础 macOS SwiftUI 应用，并添加项目内的 `script/build_and_run.sh` 入口，方便我将其连接到 `Run` 操作。\n\n约束：\n- 以 shell 为先。Xcode 项目优先使用 `xcodebuild`；以软件包为先的应用使用 `swift build`。\n- 明确建模 Mac 场景：根据产品需要选择主窗口，以及 `Settings`、`MenuBarExtra` 或工具窗口。\n- 优先使用原生桌面侧边栏、工具栏、菜单、键盘快捷键和系统材质，而不是 iOS 风格的逐页推入导航。\n- 只有当 SwiftUI 无法清楚表达桌面行为时，才使用范围有限的 AppKit 桥接。\n- 每项改动都采用一个小型验证循环，并准确告诉我运行了哪些构建、启动或日志命令。\n\n交付：\n- 应用框架或我要求的 Mac 功能片段\n- 可复用的构建与运行脚本\n- 你实际执行的最小验证步骤\n- 你建议的任何桌面专属后续工作\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">代理技能</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"scaffold-the-app-and-build-loop\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">搭建应用和构建循环</h2> <p>对于新的 Mac 应用，先请 Codex 选择恰当的场景模型：<code>WindowGroup</code>、<code>Window</code>、<code>Settings</code>、<code>MenuBarExtra</code> 或 <code>DocumentGroup</code>。这样一开始就能采用原生桌面应用结构，而不是从 iOS 风格的 <code>ContentView</code> 慢慢演变。</p> <p>保持执行循环以 shell 为先。Xcode 项目使用 <code>xcodebuild</code>；以软件包为先的项目使用 <code>swift build</code> 和项目内的 <code>script/build_and_run.sh</code> 封装脚本。该脚本应能停止旧进程、构建应用并启动新产物，还可按需显示日志或遥测信息。</p> <p>如果纯 SwiftPM 应用是图形界面应用，请将它打包并作为 <code>.app</code> 启动，而不是直接运行原始可执行文件。这样可以避免本地验证时出现 Dock、激活状态和应用包标识相关问题。</p> <p><a id=\"leverage-skills\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">使用技能</h2> <p>随着工作越来越偏向桌面，在适当时候加入 <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps 插件（需联网）</a>。它涵盖以 shell 为先的构建和调试循环、SwiftPM 应用打包、原生 SwiftUI 场景和窗口模式、AppKit 互操作、统一日志、测试问题分类以及签名/公证工作流。</p> <p>如需进一步了解，请参阅<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">插件文档（本地尚未收录）</a>和<a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">技能文档（本地尚未收录）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"build-desktop-native-ui\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">构建原生桌面界面</h2> <p>优先遵循 Mac 惯例，而不是 iOS 导航模式。如果侧边栏/详情布局适合该功能，就使用 <code>NavigationSplitView</code>；偏好设置应放在明确的 <code>Settings</code> 场景中，并使用工具栏和命令提供易于发现的操作；只有适合产品时才使用菜单栏附加项来提供轻量、随时可用的工具。</p> <p>先使用系统材质、语义颜色和标准控件。只有当产品需要独特桌面界面时，才添加自定义窗口样式、拖动区域或 Liquid Glass 表面。</p> <p>如果 SwiftUI 已经接近满足需求，但还差一点，可以添加尽可能小的 AppKit 桥接。合适的例子包括打开/保存面板、第一响应者控制、菜单校验、拖放边界，以及封装一个特殊控件的 <code>NSView</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"debug-test-and-prepare-for-shipping\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">调试、测试并准备发布</h2> <p>为了验证运行时行为，可以让 Codex 在窗口打开、侧边栏选中、菜单命令或后台同步周围添加少量 <code>Logger</code> 事件；应用启动后，再通过 <code>log stream</code> 验证这些事件。</p> <p>测试失败时，先让 Codex 运行最小且有用范围的 <code>xcodebuild test</code> 或 <code>swift test</code>，再判断这是编译失败、断言失败、崩溃、偶发故障，还是环境/设置问题。</p> <p>如果工作转向分发，就同时准备在 Xcode 中手动归档的路径，以及可重复的脚本化归档和公证路径。请 Codex 检查应用包、entitlements 和 hardened runtime，可使用 <code>codesign</code> 与 <code>plutil</code>；如果需要通过上传来发布应用，再使用 <a href=\"https://asccli.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Store Connect CLI（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"example-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">示例提示词</h2> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build macOS Apps plugin to build a native macOS SwiftUI version of this app feature.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Use a desktop-native scene structure with a main window, settings, and toolbar/command actions where they make sense.\n- Prefer a sidebar/detail layout over iOS-style push navigation if the feature benefits from always-visible structure.\n- Add a tiny AppKit bridge only if SwiftUI cannot express one specific desktop behavior cleanly.\n- Create or update `script/build_and_run.sh` so the build/run loop stays shell-first.\n- Tell me which build, launch, test, and log commands you used.\n\nShip the feature slice, verify it with the smallest relevant build or test loop, and summarize any signing or packaging follow-up needed before distribution.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 Build macOS Apps 插件，为这项应用功能构建采用 SwiftUI 的原生 macOS 版本。\n\n约束：\n\n- 采用桌面原生的场景结构，在适当位置提供主窗口、设置，以及工具栏或命令操作。\n- 如果持续可见的结构有助于使用这项功能，优先采用侧栏与详情布局，而不是 iOS 风格的逐层推进导航。\n- 只有在 SwiftUI 无法清晰表达某项具体桌面行为时，才添加一个小型 AppKit 桥接层。\n- 创建或更新 `script/build_and_run.sh`，让构建与运行循环继续以 Shell 为主要入口。\n- 告诉我你使用了哪些构建、启动、测试和日志命令。\n\n交付这部分功能，用与其相关的最小构建或测试循环验证，并总结分发之前还需要完成的签名或打包工作。</div></div> <p><a id=\"practical-tips\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_11\">实用建议</h2> <p><a id=\"keep-scenes-explicit\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">明确划分场景</h3> <p>将主窗口、设置窗口、工具窗口和菜单栏附加项分别建模为独立场景入口，而不是把整个应用塞进一个巨大的视图中。</p> <p><a id=\"let-system-chrome-do-more-of-the-work\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">让系统界面承担更多工作</h3> <p>在创建自定义侧边栏、工具栏或材质之前，先检查标准 SwiftUI 场景与窗口 API 是否已经能提供你需要的 Mac 行为。</p> <p><a id=\"treat-appkit-as-a-narrow-edge\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"appkit\">将 AppKit 限定在少数缺口上</h3> <p>使用 <code>NSViewRepresentable</code>、<code>NSViewControllerRepresentable</code> 或专用的 <code>NSWindow</code> 辅助代码补上一个缺少的桌面能力，但仍以 SwiftUI 作为选中状态和应用状态的唯一事实来源。</p> <p><a id=\"validate-signing-and-notarization-separately-from-local-build-success\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">将签名和公证与本地构建成功分开验证</h3> <p>本地成功启动并不能证明应用已正确签名或已达到公证要求。如果任务涉及发布，就保留手动 Xcode 归档流程，同时添加脚本化归档与公证流程以便重复执行；只有当任务确实涉及发布时，才检查 <code>codesign</code> 和 <code>plutil</code>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-for-macos\">Build for macOS</h1> <p>Use Codex to scaffold, build, and debug native Mac apps with SwiftUI.</p> <p>Use Codex to build macOS SwiftUI apps, wire a shell-first build-and-run loop, and add desktop-native scene, window, AppKit, and signing workflows as the app matures.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Greenfield macOS SwiftUI apps where you want Codex to scaffold a desktop-native app shell and repeatable build script</li> <li>Existing Mac apps where Codex needs to work on windows, menus, sidebars, settings, AppKit interop, or signing issues</li> <li>Teams that want macOS work to stay shell-first while still respecting native desktop UX conventions</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">build-macos-apps (online)</a></td> <td>Build and debug macOS apps with shell-first workflows, design desktop-native SwiftUI scenes and windows, bridge to AppKit where needed, and prepare signing and notarization paths.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>UI framework</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/swiftui/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SwiftUI (online)</a></td> <td>A strong default for windows, sidebars, toolbars, settings, and scene-driven Mac app structure.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>AppKit bridge</td> <td><a href=\"https://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AppKit (online)</a></td> <td>Use small <code>NSViewRepresentable</code>, <code>NSViewControllerRepresentable</code>, or <code>NSWindow</code> bridges when SwiftUI stops short of a desktop behavior you need.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Build and packaging</td> <td><code>xcodebuild</code>, <code>swift build</code>, and <a href=\"https://asccli.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Store Connect CLI (online)</a></td> <td>Keep local builds, manual archives, script-based notarization, and App Store uploads in a repeatable terminal-first loop.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Scaffold a Native Mac App</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build macOS Apps plugin to scaffold a starter macOS SwiftUI app and add a project-local `script/build_and_run.sh` entrypoint I can wire to a `Run` action.\n\nConstraints:\n- Stay shell-first. Prefer `xcodebuild` for Xcode projects and `swift build` for package-first apps.\n- Model Mac scenes explicitly with a main window plus `Settings`, `MenuBarExtra`, or utility windows only when they fit the product.\n- Prefer desktop-native sidebars, toolbars, menus, keyboard shortcuts, and system materials over iOS-style push navigation.\n- Use a narrow AppKit bridge only when SwiftUI cannot express the desktop behavior cleanly.\n- Keep one small validation loop for each change and tell me exactly which build, launch, or log commands you ran.\n\nDeliver:\n- the app scaffold or requested Mac feature slice\n- a reusable build-and-run script\n- the smallest validation steps you ran\n- any desktop-specific follow-up work you recommend\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\">Model Context Protocol</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-575ba4762ea69b23\">Agent skills</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"scaffold-the-app-and-build-loop\">Scaffold the app and build loop</h2> <p>For a new Mac app, ask Codex to choose the right scene model first: <code>WindowGroup</code>, <code>Window</code>, <code>Settings</code>, <code>MenuBarExtra</code>, or <code>DocumentGroup</code>. That keeps the app desktop-native from the first pass instead of growing from an iOS-style <code>ContentView</code>.</p> <p>Keep the execution loop shell-first. For Xcode projects, use <code>xcodebuild</code>. For package-first apps, use <code>swift build</code> and a project-local <code>script/build_and_run.sh</code> wrapper that stops the old process, builds the app, launches the new artifact, and can optionally expose logs or telemetry.</p> <p>If a pure SwiftPM app is a GUI app, bundle and launch it as a <code>.app</code> instead of running the raw executable directly. That avoids missing Dock, activation, and bundle-identity issues during local validation.</p> <h2 id=\"leverage-skills\">Leverage skills</h2> <p>Add the <a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/build-macos-apps\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build macOS Apps plugin (online)</a> once the work gets more desktop-specific. It covers shell-first build and debug loops, SwiftPM app packaging, native SwiftUI scene and window patterns, AppKit interop, unified logging, test triage, and signing/notarization workflows.</p> <p>To learn more about how to install and use plugins and skills, see the <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/plugins\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">plugins documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a> and <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/build-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">skills documentation (not in this local snapshot)</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"build-desktop-native-ui\">Build desktop-native UI</h2> <p>Prefer Mac conventions over iOS navigation patterns. Use <code>NavigationSplitView</code> for sidebar/detail layouts, explicit <code>Settings</code> scenes for preferences, toolbars and commands for discoverable actions, and menu bar extras for lightweight always-available utilities.</p> <p>Use system materials, semantic colors, and standard controls first. Add custom window styling, drag regions, or Liquid Glass surfaces only when the product needs a distinct desktop surface.</p> <p>If SwiftUI gets close but not all the way there, add the smallest possible AppKit bridge. Good examples are open/save panels, first-responder control, menu validation, drag-and-drop edges, and a wrapped <code>NSView</code> for one specialized control.</p> <h2 id=\"debug-test-and-prepare-for-shipping\">Debug, test, and prepare for shipping</h2> <p>For runtime behavior, ask Codex to add a few <code>Logger</code> events around window opening, sidebar selection, menu commands, or background sync, then verify those events with <code>log stream</code> after the app launches.</p> <p>For failing tests, have Codex run the smallest useful <code>xcodebuild test</code> or <code>swift test</code> scope first and classify whether the issue is compilation, an assertion failure, a crash, a flake, or an environment/setup problem.</p> <p>When the work shifts from local iteration to distribution, ask Codex to prepare both a manual archive path in Xcode and a script-based archive and notarization path for repeatable shipping. Have it inspect the app bundle, entitlements, and hardened runtime with <code>codesign</code> and <code>plutil</code>, and use <a href=\"https://asccli.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">App Store Connect CLI (online)</a> when you want uploads to stay in the terminal too.</p> <h2 id=\"example-prompt\">Example prompt</h2> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Build macOS Apps plugin to build a native macOS SwiftUI version of this app feature.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Use a desktop-native scene structure with a main window, settings, and toolbar/command actions where they make sense.\n- Prefer a sidebar/detail layout over iOS-style push navigation if the feature benefits from always-visible structure.\n- Add a tiny AppKit bridge only if SwiftUI cannot express one specific desktop behavior cleanly.\n- Create or update `script/build_and_run.sh` so the build/run loop stays shell-first.\n- Tell me which build, launch, test, and log commands you used.\n\nShip the feature slice, verify it with the smallest relevant build or test loop, and summarize any signing or packaging follow-up needed before distribution.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"practical-tips\">Practical tips</h2> <h3 id=\"keep-scenes-explicit\">Keep scenes explicit</h3> <p>Model the main window, settings window, utility windows, and menu bar extras as separate scene roots instead of hiding the whole app inside one giant view.</p> <h3 id=\"let-system-chrome-do-more-of-the-work\">Let system chrome do more of the work</h3> <p>Before creating custom sidebars, toolbars, or materials, check whether standard SwiftUI scene and window APIs already give you the Mac behavior you want.</p> <h3 id=\"treat-appkit-as-a-narrow-edge\">Treat AppKit as a narrow edge</h3> <p>Use <code>NSViewRepresentable</code>, <code>NSViewControllerRepresentable</code>, or a focused <code>NSWindow</code> helper for one missing desktop capability, but keep SwiftUI as the source of truth for selection and app state.</p> <h3 id=\"validate-signing-and-notarization-separately-from-local-build-success\">Validate signing and notarization separately from local build success</h3> <p>A successful local launch does not prove the app is signed or notarization-ready. Keep a manual Xcode archive flow for one-off release checks, add a scripted archive and notarization flow for repeatable distribution, and run <code>codesign</code> and <code>plutil</code> checks when the task is about shipping, not just local iteration.</p>"};
